      "discriminatedBy": {
        "param": "path",
        "rule": "Selected when the attachment source is passed as a Text pathname/file name."
      }
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "If name is omitted: when the source is a file/path, the file's own name and extension are used; when the source is a BLOB or ZipFile, a random name without extension is generated.",
    "If type is omitted or an empty string, the content-type is inferred from the attachment's file extension (per the documented extension-to-MIME-type table); an explicit type overrides this regardless of extension.",
    "If disposition is omitted: it defaults to \"inline\" when a non-empty cid is passed, otherwise it defaults to \"attachment\".",
    "cid may be passed as an empty string to explicitly opt out of the Content-Id header.",
    "Reference lifecycle (implied convention, not syntactically enforced): Mail message building: MAIL New attachment creates attachment objects to add into an Email object's attachments collection -> MAIL Convert to MIME serializes the completed email object to MIME text (used internally by SMTP_transporter.send()) -> MAIL Convert from MIME parses an inbound MIME document back into an email object."
  ]
